WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.160
The 2018 superhero body count was impressive,
and 2019's butcher's bill promises to stack

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.310
at least as high.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.540
Last year, the genre didn't really give us
impressive numbers until the release of Avengers:

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.540
Infinity War.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.240
Meanwhile, the ranks of the capes have already
been seriously thinned in 2019.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.920
Warning: Spoilers ahead

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:22.040
First appearing in 2016's Suicide Squad #3,
the bizarre Cosmonut was a member of Russia's

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.339
Annihilation Brigade.

00:00:23.339 --> 00:00:27.409
The Brigade tried and failed to stop the Squad
from escaping after they broke into an underground

00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:28.409
prison.

00:00:28.409 --> 00:00:32.689
But in Suicide Squad #50, Cosmonut sacrificed
himself for his old adversaries.

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:36.560
With Amanda Waller rendered a giant, mindless
beast that could breathe fire, Harley Quinn

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.730
and Rick Flag were not much of a match.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.930
In an uncharacteristic move, Cosmonut saved
his old enemies by holding off Waller.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.329
Quinn and Flag eventually managed to find
the rest of the Squad and restore Waller to

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:49.060
her old form, but not in time to save Cosmonut.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.390
Before losing her powers, Waller melted his
big metal hammer head.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.920
“Damn, that is just one mean lady.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.840
“Yeah”

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.780
Glass saw all of its super-guys killed in
a single scene.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.610
Unfortunately, that includes David Dunn, who
had been known as the vigilante Overseer since

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:05.820
2000's Unbreakable.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:09.520
In the final battle between Dunn and the Beast,
the latter - having learned from Elijah that

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.820
Dunn's weakness is water - hurls himself and
Dunn into a huge plastic water tank.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:17.520
The tank proves too brittle for the struggle
and shatters, freeing them both and flooding

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.750
a large pothole.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:22.360
After Dunn's son Joseph begs policemen to
help his father, one of the policemen shoves

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:23.540
Dunn's face into the pothole.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.710
Dr. Ellie Staple rushes to Dunn and tells
him to hold her hand.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.259
He does, and his power allows him to see a
memory of Staple's, a meeting of a secret

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:33.140
society dedicated to keeping people with powers
in check.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.350
She tells Dunn if she'd convinced him that
he never had powers, he would've been allowed

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:37.350
to live.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.960
The policeman pushes Dunn's face back into
the water, drowning him.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.720
"A lot of people are going to die."

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.840
A star athlete paralyzed by a bullet during
a peaceful protest, Khalil Payne fell under

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.659
the sway of the power-hungry Tobias Whale,
who funded surgery that restored Khalil's

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:51.869
ability to walk and gave him powers.

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:55.590
Whale treated Khalil like a son at first,
and in return Khalil served Whale as Painkiller.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.689
He used poisoned darts to attack random former
classmates, eventually fighting and defeating

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:01.180
Black Lightning himself.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.759
After Whale's treatment of Khalil turns ugly
and abusive, Khalil finally finds the courage

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:07.789
to turn on Whale and run away with his ex-girlfriend
Jen.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:11.290
Khalil agrees to go home, turn himself in,
and enter witness protection.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:15.400
Whale hijacks Khalil's transport and confronts
his former protege, ripping Khalil's cybernetic

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.849
spine out of his back with his bare hands.

00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:22.040
While Khalil clings to life following Whale's
brutal attack, Jen convinces her psychic teacher,

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.340
Perenna, to ease Khalil's passing by placing
the couple in a dream world where they're

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.560
on their way to the prom.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:32.080
February's Uncanny X-Men #11 represented the
first reunion of Cyclops and the newly resurrected

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:33.090
Wolverine.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.540
But while it gave the X-Men back two of their
favorite sons, it also stole away two lesser-known

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:37.540
daughters.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.580
The first victim was the young, future-seeing
Blindfold, real name Ruth.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:44.600
In the wake of almost all of the X-Men disappearing
in previous issues, Blindfold was one of the

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.849
few allies both Wolverine and Cyclops were
able to contact while looking for survivors.

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:52.920
Unfortunately, she was seeing bleak and disturbing
images of the future, causing her to feel

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.019
utterly hopeless.

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:57.800
Scott Summers finds Ruth has committed suicide
in her bathtub, cryptically writing "This

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.610
is forever" on the wall in her own blood.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:03.879
Ruth first entered the X-Men mythos courtesy
of Buffy the Vampire Slayer creator Joss Whedon

00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:07.810
and artist John Cassaday's game-changing Astonishing
X-Men run, when Ruth predicted the tragic

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.200
suicide of fellow Xavier student Wing.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.680
Loa's death is portrayed strangely, particularly
for a superhero character.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.970
We see little of the events leading up to
it, don't know who killed Loa or how it happened.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.080
Held hostage by Blindfold's random "memory"
of what has happened, what is happening, and

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:26.659
what's to come, we find Velocidad and Blindfold
standing over the corpse of Loa in the snow.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:29.599
We don't know exactly how she died or exactly
who killed her.

00:03:29.599 --> 00:03:34.050
Considering the events of the rest of Uncanny
X-Men #11, which shows how jubilant anti-mutant

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:38.040
groups like the Purifiers are in the wake
of the X-Men's disappearance, it seems likely

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.120
a mutant-hating group was responsible for
Loa's death, but we don't know for sure.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.880
The feel of the issue, particularly Blindfold's
chapter, suggests the confusion will be cleared

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.800
up soon.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:51.471
As The Gifted's second season reaches its
climax, Marcos, a.k.a. Eclipse, meant to capture

00:03:51.471 --> 00:03:55.530
and interrogate Inner Circle stooge Max about
the group's plans, but Max fights back and

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.470
forces Marcos to use deadly force.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.769
That leads Inner Circle head Reeva to search
for the traitor who led the Mutant Underground

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:01.769
to Max.

00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:03.090
She blames the wrong person.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.640
Not knowing that Polaris has learned to use
her magnetic powers to hack computer systems,

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.909
Reeva and the Frost sisters blame Sage, whose
powers revolve around computer systems and

00:04:10.909 --> 00:04:12.460
whose digital signature they find.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:15.269
Sage pleads her innocence, but Reeva is unconvinced.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:18.860
She uses her sonic powers with her usual mercilessness,
killing Sage.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.690
While Sage is innocent of betraying the Inner
Circle in The Gifted, her comic book counterpart

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:26.240
was a spy for Professor X, infiltrating the
infamous Hellfire Club.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.200
Early in the current run of Batman, the Caped
Crusader comes across two heroes he thinks

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.950
might act as replacements in his mission to
safeguard Gotham.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:37.050
The brother/sister team of Gotham and Gotham
Girl have Superman-like powers and idolized

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.050
Batman.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:40.820
They'd subjected themselves to experiments
to gain their powers, and those powers were

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.280
slowly killing them.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.100
Gotham dies and Batman does what he could
to help Gotham Girl.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:49.230
In the mini-event "The Price," Gotham Girl
returns with a plan for vengeance, a mystery

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.390
benefactor, and her brother resurrected.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.030
Gotham's return is short-lived, though.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.880
In battle with the Flash, Gotham quickly overextends
himself and again dies, literally exploding.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:02.680
If Blindfold and Loa weren't enough, the following
week in Uncanny X-Men #12, former X-Factor

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.970
member Guido, a.k.a.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.350
Strong Guy, falls.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:08.760
Still looking for surviving X-Men, Cyclops
and Wolverine learn that mutants were being

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.550
imprisoned and used to power a new kind of
Sentinel.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:15.380
Freeing Strong Guy, Mirage, and others from
their Sentinel suits, Cyclops and Wolverine

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.930
lead a raid on the prison to free the remaining
mutants.

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:21.560
On their way out of the prison, a copy of
Multiple Man discovers he had been booby trapped

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:22.560
with a bomb.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.620
Guido uses his body to absorb the blast and
protect his allies.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:29.320
Already weakened by a techno-organic virus,
Guido didn't survive the blast.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.510
Still being pursued, the X-Men were forced
to leave their friend's massive body behind.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.510
Reed Strucker (The Gifted) February 26, 2019

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:36.850
When active, Reed Strucker's powers caused
anything he touched to disintegrate, which

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:40.490
unintentionally jeopardized his own safety
and that of everyone around him.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:43.900
He'd managed to use his powers consciously
once or twice, but for the most part they

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:45.090
eluded his control.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.210
He went so far as to suppress them with drugs.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.000
"I have this ability and there's nothing I
can do with it."

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.690
In the season finale, Reed uses his lack of
control to a noble end.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:57.400
When the Mutant Underground raids the Inner
Circle's headquarters to stop Reeva from sparking

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.070
a mutant/human war, Reed slips past her security
and confronts her.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.900
Knowing Reeva's sonic powers would make his
abilities even more unpredictable, Reed cuts

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.750
loose, utterly destroying the top floors of
the Inner Circle's building, killing himself

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.080
and Reeva in the process.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:14.150
Most readers knew one team member would bite
the dust by the end of X-Force #4.

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:18.160
Previews of the cover showed the teenage Cable
cradling what appeared to be an obscured corpse.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.940
The obvious choice was Deathlok who appeared
mortally wounded by the mutant-hunting Ahab

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.190
in the previous issue.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.510
Deathlok gets better, though.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:28.880
Then Ahab nearly disembowels Shatterstar with
Wolverine-ish claws he'd taken from Deathlok.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:32.061
But Shatterstar gets better, too, and it looks
like the cover might've just been big one

00:06:32.061 --> 00:06:33.061
big tease.

00:06:33.061 --> 00:06:36.970
Ahab and his mutant-hating ally are both dead
when finally, on the second-to-last page,

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:40.280
an energy portal appears behind Warpath and
he's impaled through the chest by some kind

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.470
of energized rod.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:45.351
Warpath collapses to the ground and the final
page reveals a splash of X-Force's old enemy

00:06:45.351 --> 00:06:49.440
Stryfe emerging from the portal, presumably
ready to send the rest of X-Force to join

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.080
Warpath in the afterlife.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.840
Asgardians of the Galaxy has proven to be
a lot of fun.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:58.620
A team of Asgardian and Asgardian-themed heroes
forms to stop Nebula from bringing about universal

00:06:58.620 --> 00:06:59.620
Ragnarok.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:03.480
The Asgardians are led by the deadly Angela
and includes Skurge the Executioner; Valkyrie;

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.000
Thunderstrike; and Throg, Frog of Thunder.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.910
The team also included the deadly Destroyer
armor, and by the end of the first issue it

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:13.730
was revealed that the armor was hiding and
protecting Kid Loki, a younger and even more

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:18.130
insufferable version who emerged as a result
of the original Loki's death in 2010.

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:22.300
There is some mystery behind how Kid Loki
dies in Asgardians of the Galaxy #7, because

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.500
it isn't a result of that issue's events.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.080
Angela finds Kid Loki lounging on the branch
of a tree.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:30.110
He tells her he can't go with her because
his older counterpart - who did eventually

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.110
return - has dismissed the spell that brought
him into being.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.360
Kid Loki simply vanishes into nothing.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.550
War of the Realms #1 ends with a major Asgardian
death.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:42.570
As Malekith's forces finally attack Earth
and the heroes of New York City rally, King

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:46.420
Laufey of the Frost Giants targets Freyja,
mother of Thor and wife of Odin.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.380
The giant has the Asgardian queen trapped
when Loki appears and separates his biological

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.440
dad's hand from the rest of his arm with a
glowing green sword.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:57.810
Calling Loki his, quote, "one great shame,"
Laufey seizes his son and devours him.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:02.030
Loki's presumed death here seems particularly
unceremonious for a character this popular,

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:05.510
not to mention the fact that he's just started
appearing in a kind of "buddy cop" miniseries

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:09.170
with Wolverine called Wolverine: Infinity
Watch, which isn't even halfway through its

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.170
run yet.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:12.200
Plus, Loki's getting a new solo series in
July.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:16.720
In Avengers: Endgame, Black Widow and Hawkeye
are half of the team sent back to 2014, where

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:18.380
they're assigned to get the Soul Stone.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:21.930
Though Nebula gives the Avengers the location
of the Soul Stone, she unfortunately doesn't

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.800
know what it will take to claim it.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.200
"The stone demands a sacrifice."

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.390
Widow and Hawkeye arrive on Vormir and quickly
encounter the Red Skull.

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:34.370
When he explains the Stone's price, Clint
and Natasha argue over who should die.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:37.750
Clint feels his actions as Ronin have turned
him into a monster, while Nat doesn't see

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.400
anything worth living for beyond the found
family Thanos' purge stole from her.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:44.550
The argument turns physical, with Clint throwing
himself over the cliff.

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:48.400
Widow follows him and winds up dangling over
a fatal drop with only Clint's grip keeping

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.400
her from falling.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.620
She begs Clint to let her go, and she eventually
falls to her death.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.280
Just like Thanos in Infinity War, Clint wakes
in a shallow pool with the Soul Stone.

00:08:56.280 --> 00:09:00.160
Early in Avengers: Endgame's final battle,
Tony Stark asks Doctor Strange if this was

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:03.080
the possible outcome Strange saw in which
the good guys win.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:04.640
"How many do we win?"

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.480
"One."

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:12.640
Strange refuses to answer at first.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.970
After Thanos captures the new Infinity Gauntlet,
Strange mutely signals to Tony with one index

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:17.970
finger.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.210
Stark rushes Thanos, who easily brushes him
aside.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:24.240
But once Thanos snaps, we learn that the point
of Tony's attack was to steal the Stones.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:27.440
Showing the gathered Stones on his suit's
gauntlet, Stark snaps his fingers and the

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.320
Mad Titan's forces turn to dust.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:32.140
Thanos slumps to the ground and is purged
from existence.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:34.700
Tony doesn't have the strength to survive
using the stones.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.050
As he struggles, Pepper summons the courage
to smile and tell him they're all going to

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.780
be fine, and that he can rest now.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:43.180
Tony dies and the light in the Arc Reactor
in his chest blinks out.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.680
At the end of the credits, you can hear Tony's
hammer striking the anvil while making his

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.960
first suit in 2008's Iron Man.

